Subject: wmp: support IWMPPlayer2 ActiveX hosts and embedded video playback
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Modification date: 2026-10-25

ActiveX hosts query IWMPPlayer2, configure the control, and may set the
same client site again after in-place activation. Provide the IDL-generated
interface and preserve the active child window across this repeated site
binding. Track enabled/context-menu and playback state, support pause and
idempotent close, and parent/resize the DirectShow video window with the
control.

For embedded playback with winemac.drv, pre-add VMR9 so video owns a
Direct3D child surface alongside the host's graphics surface. Other drivers
retain normal DirectShow renderer selection. Selection depends on the
active driver and hosting mode and applies to all matching applications.

The standalone WMP probe exercises interface properties, ATL site rebinding,
child-window visibility, playback progress, and repeated close on x86/x64.
Playback requires a caller-supplied video path. Native WMP skins, fullscreen,
and true windowless video remain outside this patch's implementation scope.

